				    #"Replaced Value1" = Table.ReplaceValue(#"Replaced Value","H2 break-off: NULL (CI includes 0); observed effect (1.815 pp) < MDE (4.270 pp): experiment could not have detected it","The commitment statement showed no reliable effect on web break-off â€” if anything, break-off ticked up in the treatment arm (+1.82 pp, 95% CI [âˆ’1.17, +4.80]), but the whole interval sits inside the experiment's 4.27 pp blind spot. An underpowered null, not a signal in either direction.",Replacer.ReplaceText,{"verdict_vis"}),
				    #"Replaced Value2" = Table.ReplaceValue(#"Replaced Value1","H3 response error: NULL (CI includes 0); observed effect (0.021 pp) < MDE (0.118 pp): experiment could not have detected it","The commitment statement showed no measurable effect on response error (âˆ’0.02 pp, 95% CI [âˆ’0.10, +0.06]) against a 0.36% baseline. Underpowered by convention, not by the plan's rule: the plan's 3 pp informativeness bar was written for far more common outcomes and doesn't scale down to one this rare â€” 'informative' vs. 'underpowered' isn't really decidable here.",Replacer.ReplaceText,{"verdict_vis"}),
				    #"Replaced Value3" = Table.ReplaceValue(#"Replaced Value2","The commitment statement did not reduce item nonresponse (âˆ’0.21 pp, 95% CI [âˆ’0.44, +0.01]). This is an informative null: the experiment could detect effects as small as 0.32 pp â€” well under the plan's 3 pp bar for a meaningful result â€” so a real effect of practical size would have shown up here.","No effect on item nonresponse (âˆ’0.21 pp). The study could reliably detect changes this small â€” this is a real null, not an inconclusive test.",Replacer.ReplaceText,{"verdict_vis"}),
				    #"Replaced Value4" = Table.ReplaceValue(#"Replaced Value3","The commitment statement showed no reliable effect on web break-off â€” if anything, break-off ticked up in the treatment arm (+1.82 pp, 95% CI [âˆ’1.17, +4.80]), but the whole interval sits inside the experiment's 4.27 pp blind spot. An underpowered null, not a signal in either direction.","No reliable effect on web break-off. If anything it rose slightly (+1.82 pp), but couldn't confirm or rule out an effect.",Replacer.ReplaceText,{"verdict_vis"}),
